{
  "about": "As tiny-chao-garden, from power-on with nothing saved to Tiny Chao Garden; then the hand goes up to the right icon and A opens its card game. Signs show what each ring of the board pays, seven pairs of cards are dealt face up and turn face down from the middle out, and the Chao walks the board pushing some of them; A while it walks left has it stop and peek at the card it's pushing. Then the hand picks: A on an empty place and A twice on one card do nothing, two cards that differ are a mistake, and the hand goes round every edge of the board as it finds the seven pairs, each paying where its cards lay. CLEAR! falls in, the two mistakes not made pay 30 rings more, and the screen fades back to the garden, its ring count up by what was won.",
